---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

import { OPERATOR, ANALYTICS } from '../../site.config.mjs';

const UPDATED = '2026-08-10';

/**
 * Read from the same constant that decides whether `Base.astro` emits the
 * script, so this page cannot claim analytics the build does not ship — or
 * stay silent about analytics it does.
 */
const analytics = ANALYTICS === 'vercel';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — Price Per Token"
  description="What Price Per Token does and does not collect. Prompts are tokenized in your browser and never uploaded."
  breadcrumbs={[['Privacy', '/privacy/']]}
>
  <section class="wrap page">
    <span class="eyebrow">Last updated {UPDATED}</span>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    <h2>Your prompt stays in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      The token counter runs entirely client-side. Text you paste is tokenized
      by JavaScript on your own machine and is never transmitted, logged, or
      stored. There is no server that could receive it.
    </p>

    <h2>What the site stores</h2>
    <p>
      No cookies, no local storage, no login, no account. Pages are static
      files{analytics ? ', and nothing you type is part of what is measured' : ''}.
    </p>

    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <p>
      Web fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, which receives your IP address as
      part of that request — standard for any site using their CDN. The site is
      served by a hosting provider that keeps ordinary server logs, typically IP
      address, timestamp, and requested URL, under its own retention policy.
    </p>
    {analytics && (
      <p>
        Page views are counted with Vercel Web Analytics, which is part of the
        hosting rather than a separate company. It sets no cookies and reads no
        local storage. Each view records the page URL, the referring URL, and
        coarse browser, operating system, device and country fields derived
        from the request; the identifier it uses to tell one visit from another
        is a hash that is discarded daily and never crosses to another site.
        Google Analytics was considered and rejected for this page: it would
        set cookies, which would make the paragraph above false.
      </p>
    )}
    <p>
      Pricing data is fetched at build time, not from your browser. No request
      you make here reaches an AI provider{
        analytics ? ', and no prompt text reaches the analytics endpoint' : ''
      }.
    </p>

    <h2>If that changes</h2>
    <p>
      Adding advertising or affiliate tracking would change what is collected.
      If that happens, this page is updated first and the date above changes
      with it.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy go to {OPERATOR} via the
      {' '}<a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="disclaimer">
      This page describes the site's actual behaviour in plain terms. It is not
      legal advice, and if you operate this site in a jurisdiction with specific
      disclosure requirements, have it reviewed.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 3rem; max-width: 62ch; }
  h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  p { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .disclaimer {
    margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--ink-faint);
  }
</style>
